 "title": "Pick and place · Level 1: four balls to spots whose coordinates are given",
 "brief": "Move the four balls from the tray to the four spots. The robot stands at (600, 600) facing 180 deg (the tray behind it, at world bearing 0); its base turns, its arm stays in one plane. The tray (80 x 300 mm, 60 mm high) holds the balls (40 mm, 30 g) on the 254.5 mm ring at world bearings -30, -10, 10 and 30 deg. The spots are 40 x 40 mm with tops of 20 (s1), 40 (s2), 60 (s3) and 80 mm (s4); each run moves them a little, and the runner fills in spots.json: keys p1 .. p4 (s1 .. s4), each [[x, y]] in mm. Per ball: 10 within 10 mm of a spot's centre, 5 within 25; -5 for a drop (a ball touching the floor), -5 for each collision of the arm with the tray; + 20 x min(1, par / t) when all four are within 25 mm before the limit. Run score = 100 x points / 60 (floor 0). Pass: a mean of 60 and at least 8 of 10 runs finishing.",
